      "phase": "preparation",
      "plan": {
        "A": "Build a parse-once graph representation with a first-match ID-to-index lookup and adjacency arrays that retain input order. Replace repeated linear searches and recursive recomputation with demand-driven memoized DFS, caching each node’s float result once. Preserve the reference’s neighbor-selection rule exactly: start at 0, update only on a strictly greater neighbor value, and keep the first neighbor on ties; ignore missing IDs and preserve the -1 recursion-sentinel behavior. Keep the DAG assumption, root order, original root token in output, and six-decimal formatting. Measure this candidate independently.",
        "B": "Explore an independent iterative alternative: choose each node’s successor by scanning its neighbors in input order with the reference’s strict-greater-than-from-zero rule, then evaluate results in reverse topological order so each node is computed once without recursive calls. Use an ID mapping that preserves lookup behavior, and retain float arithmetic and the reference’s -1 sentinel behavior. Compare runtime and output against the baseline and A; computing every node may cost more on small or sparsely queried graphs, so measure rather than assume a win.",
        "C": "Test parallel evaluation as a separate, cautious experiment for the 4-core ARM64 target. After selecting successors, process the resulting acyclic dependencies by reverse topological levels, parallelizing only independent nodes within a level. Keep a serial path for workloads where measurements show parallel overhead dominates; choose any crossover from general workload measurements, not test-specific assumptions. Avoid shared-cache races and preserve output order and exact selection/formatting semantics. Reject the approach if end-to-end measurements regress.",
        "G": "Integrate only candidates that pass the existing correctness checks, and benchmark each standalone before considering combinations. Select by measured end-to-end performance; do not assume improvements add, and remeasure any integrated combination. Preserve stdin/stdout behavior, root order, reference selection and float semantics, and output formatting. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or other protected experiment inputs.",
        "analysis": "The only automatic result is a correct baseline on 4 cases: mean 0.012026847 seconds (samples 0.012110462, 0.011953024, 0.012017054), score 0.50, on a 4-core ARM64 target. There is no profiling or candidate-interaction evidence, so the repeated linear ID lookup and repeated recursive work are source-based hypotheses, not measured bottlenecks. The three lanes test distinct approaches—memoized DFS, iterative DP, and parallel level processing—while retaining the reference’s neighbor order, strict comparison, zero initial maximum, and output behavior for every valid input."
      },
